IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch2`
IMPORT `kn-majority`
IMPORT `kn-seat`

-- Mishnah Kinnim: WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT.
-- At least one case for every question in kn-seat.l4: a person stating facts, and the answer the text
-- gives.  Every expected value was written from the text (or the named commentator) before the file
-- was run.  Counts are of BIRDS unless the line says pairs.  Target compiler: main.

§ `Kinnim: worked cases for the person who brought the birds`

§§ `Where on the altar, and what I vowed (1:1)`

-- My bird sin offering was made above the line: not valid.
#ASSERT NOT (`was my offering made at the right place on the altar` bird `sin offering` above)
-- My bird burnt offering was made above: valid.
#ASSERT `was my offering made at the right place on the altar` bird `burnt offering` above
-- I said "I take a burnt offering upon me": a vow; my bird then died: I must bring another.
#ASSERT `did my words make a vow or a gift` `it is upon me` EQUALS vow
#ASSERT `must I replace my bird that died or was stolen` vow EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I said "this one is a burnt offering": a gift; it was stolen: I need not.
#ASSERT `must I replace my bird that died or was stolen` (`did my words make a vow or a gift` `this one is`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- My obligation's bird died: this unit does not say.
#ASSERT `must I replace my bird that died or was stolen` obligation EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Mixed, the priest asking first (1:2 to 1:4, 3:5)`

-- My one pair was mixed with another woman's one pair: half may be offered, two birds of four.
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 0 0 1 (LIST 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2
-- My one pair among others' two, three, ten and a hundred: the fewest, one pair (two birds).
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 0 0 1 (LIST 2, 3, 10, 100) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2
-- My hundred pairs among others' one, two, three and ten: still one pair.
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 0 0 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2
-- We bought our two pairs jointly (Rabbi Yose): nothing is lost, all four may be offered.
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 0 0 1 (LIST 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS 4
-- A bird already made a sin offering fell among my two pairs: two birds, as sin offerings.
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 1 0 2 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2
-- A sin offering and a burnt offering, both already assigned, were mixed: none.
#ASSERT `how many of the mixed birds may still be offered` 1 1 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- 3:5: one of my two pairs' burnt offerings was already made, so I owe two sin offerings and one burnt
-- offering; a sin offering fell in: two may be offered (half of four).
#ASSERT `how many may be offered when a designated bird fell among what I still owe` `sin offering` 2 1 EQUALS 2
-- I owe one sin offering and two burnt offerings, and a sin offering fell in: one.
#ASSERT `how many may be offered when a designated bird fell among what I still owe` `sin offering` 1 2 EQUALS 1

§§ `A bird flew (2:1 to 2:5)`

#ASSERT `what now that one bird of my pair has gone` `into the air` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
#ASSERT `what now that one bird of my pair has gone` `among birds that are to be offered` EQUALS `the bird that flew is invalid and invalidates one bird where it landed`
-- Two pairs and two pairs: a bird went over and came back: two pairs of the four.
#ASSERT `how many of our four pairs can still be offered` 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `how many of our four pairs can still be offered` 1 EQUALS 3
-- I am the seventh, with seven pairs; one round trip: six; three: four ("some say": five).
#ASSERT `how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 7 1 FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 7 3 FALSE EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 7 3 TRUE EQUALS 5
-- I am the fourth, with four pairs; one round trip: two; two round trips: nothing.
#ASSERT `how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 4 1 FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `how many of my pairs in the row can still be offered` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 4 2 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `what now that a bird flew between my pair and an assigned pair` `one flew from the unassigned pair to the designated pair` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
#ASSERT `what now that my pair in the middle flew` `one flew from the middle to each side` EQUALS `nothing is lost`
#ASSERT `what now that my pair in the middle flew` `then one flew from the middle to a side` EQUALS `all of them die`

§§ `Two species, and heirs (2:5)`

-- My sin offering a young pigeon, my burnt offering a turtledove: bring a burnt offering, a young pigeon.
#ASSERT `what must I bring again for my pair of two species` `young pigeon` turtledove TRUE `the first view` EQUALS `bring again` `burnt offering` `young pigeon`
-- The same, my burnt offering brought first, as Ben Azzai: bring a sin offering, a turtledove.
#ASSERT `what must I bring again for my pair of two species` `young pigeon` turtledove FALSE `Ben Azzai` EQUALS `bring again` `sin offering` turtledove
-- My mother brought her sin offering and died: I bring her burnt offering.  Her burnt offering: I do not
-- bring her sin offering.
#ASSERT `must I as heir bring the other offering` `sin offering`
#ASSERT NOT (`must I as heir bring the other offering` `burnt offering`)

§§ `Mixed, the priest not asking (3:1 to 3:4)`

-- Three pairs and three, half above and half below: half, six of twelve.
#ASSERT `at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` 3 (LIST 3) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 6
-- The Mishnah's own case, half and half: two hundred of two hundred and thirty-two.
#ASSERT `at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 200
-- All above: half, the burnt offerings.
#ASSERT `at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) `offered all above` EQUALS JUST 116
-- Some other split: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) `offered some other number above` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reiss's Sarah, Rivkah and Leah (4, 6, 7): twenty birds, ten of each kind.
#ASSERT `at least how many of the mixed offerings counted` 4 (LIST 6, 7) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 20
-- Under Tiferet Yisrael's reading, R. Heller's 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 gives twenty; Koppel and Reiss, sixteen.
#ASSERT `at least how many counted under the reading` 1 (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5) `Tiferet Yisrael` EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `at least how many counted under the reading` 1 (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5) `Koppel and Reiss` EQUALS JUST 16
-- Under Bartenura's reading five owners are not spoken of.
#ASSERT `at least how many counted under the reading` 1 (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5) Bartenura EQUALS NOTHING
-- Pairs to bring again between us: sixteen in the Mishnah's case; one, for one pair and two.
#ASSERT `how many pairs must we bring again between us` 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `how many pairs must we bring again between us` 1 (LIST 2) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 1
-- Maimonides: my three pairs against another's two: all mine count.  My two against three: he does not say.
#ASSERT `on Maimonides' reading, did all my offerings count` 3 (LIST 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `on Maimonides' reading, did all my offerings count` 2 (LIST 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Beyond the text (Beller): one pair and two, four birds above: three.
#ASSERT `beyond the text, at least how many counted` 1 (LIST 2) 4 EQUALS JUST 3
-- A sin offering for me and a burnt offering for her, half and half: none counted.
#ASSERT `at least how many counted when assigned birds were mixed in` 1 1 EMPTY `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 0
-- 3:4: two of each assigned and one unassigned pair, half and half: two.
#ASSERT `at least how many counted when assigned birds were mixed in` 2 2 (LIST 1) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 2

§§ `My vow for the birth of a son (3:6)`

#ASSERT `how many more birds must I bring for my vow and my obligation` `she did not say which birds were for her vow` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `how many more birds must I bring for my vow and my obligation` `she said which birds were for her vow` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `how many more birds must I bring for my vow and my obligation` `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `how many more birds must I bring for my vow and my obligation` `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 8
